            <ArticleTitle>Nuclear imaging as a screening test for patients referred for intraarticular facet block.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Our experience, in a group of 25 patients with chronic low back pain, shows that nuclear imaging of the spine with 99mTc-methylene diphosphonate is of no benefit in predicting the sites at which intraarticular facet blocks may be successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
